yunohost (12.1.41.37) stable; urgency=low

  * nostrhost: postinstall creates the default operator account (single sign-in).
    - postinstall --new now creates the ``nostrhost`` admin account and links
      the operator identity to it, so the operator can sign in at the portal
      with their nsec and the admin console recognises them out of the box.
    - postinstall provisions the portal session secret
      (/etc/yunohost/.ssowat_cookie_secret, 32-byte AES-256 key) which the
      portal-api session cookie needs; without it the single sign-in flow
      could not mint sessions.
    - identity-definition events (kind 31102) can carry an ``admin`` flag so
      the projector creates the account as a YunoHost admin.
    - user_create no longer crashes on minimal installs: nscd invalidation
      tolerates a missing nscd, and the password dictionary check treats a
      missing file as not-listed.
    - user_is_allowed_on_domain checks native admin before the per-domain
      portal-settings file, so an admin can sign in before app_ssowatconf has
      written that file.

 -- NostrHost <noreply@nostrhost.org>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 18:25:29 

